WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:22.950
Blue Fins by Sarah Axton

00:25.000 --> 00:28.950
It's hot. The sun is shining.

00:29.000 --> 00:31.500
The sky is blue.

00:33.000 --> 00:37.800
The hot sun is shining in the blue sky.

00:38.000 --> 00:41.800
Jen lives in Australia.

00:42.000 --> 00:46.800
Jen and her friends are not at college today.

00:47.000 --> 00:49.800
It is the weekend.

00:50.000 --> 00:52.800
Jen is on the beach.

00:53.000 --> 00:55.950
She's standing on the hot sand.

00:57.500 --> 01:01.700
She's waving to her boyfriend, Rick.

01:01.900 --> 01:05.800
Rick and Jen's friends are in the sea.

01:06.000 --> 01:11.800
They are swimming and surfing. "Hi, Rick!"
 
01:12.000 --> 01:14.800
Rick is very happy.

01:15.000 --> 01:17.800
He has a new surfboard.

01:18.000 --> 01:21.800
The surfboard is red and white.

01:22.000 --> 01:25.800
Rick's favourite sport is surfing.

01:27.000 --> 01:29.800
"I'm going surfing."

01:30.000 --> 01:33.800
"My new surfboard is very fast."

01:34.000 --> 01:36.800
"It's great."

01:37.000 --> 01:39.100
"I'm going swimming."

01:39.200 --> 01:42.800
"I'm going to look at the fish underwater."

01:43.000 --> 01:45.800
"See you later."

01:46.000 --> 01:48.800
Jen walks along the beach.

01:49.000 --> 01:51.800
She sits on some rocks.

01:52.000 --> 01:56.800
Jen puts her blue rubber fins on her feet.

01:57.000 --> 02:02.800
She puts the yellow mask and snorkel on her face.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.800
The water is warm.

02:06.000 --> 02:09.800
Her blue fins splash loudly.

02:10.000 --> 02:12.800
Jen takes a big breath.

02:13.000 --> 02:16.800
She dives under the water.

02:17.000 --> 02:24.900
She moves her blue fins and swims very quickly.

02:25.000 --> 02:26.800
She goes down and down.

02:27.000 --> 02:32.200
She can see fish and plants.

02:32.300 --> 02:39.100
She can see fish and plants through her yellow mask.

02:39.200 --> 02:40.950
The fish and plants are very beautiful.

02:41.000 --> 02:44.800
The fish swim all around her.

02:45.000 --> 02:48.800
Jen can see yellow fish.

02:49.000 --> 02:54.900
She can see blue fish.

02:55.000 --> 02:56.800
There are green, red and white fish.

02:57.000 --> 03:00.800
Jen looks at the plants.

03:04.000 --> 03:06.950
They grow on the rocks.

03:07.100 --> 03:10.800
There are tall plants.

03:11.000 --> 03:14.800
There are small plants.

03:15.000 --> 03:17.800
Jen touches the plants.

03:18.000 --> 03:21.800
Some plants are soft.

03:22.000 --> 03:25.100
Some plants are hard.

03:25.300 --> 03:30.800
Fish live in the plants and rocks.

03:31.000 --> 03:33.950
Jen sees a sea urchin.

03:34.000 --> 03:37.800
She doesn't touch the sea urchin.
 
03:38.000 --> 03:40.800
It's dangerous.

03:41.000 --> 03:44.800
It has sharp spines.

03:45.000 --> 03:48.800
Jen swims up to get air.

03:49.000 --> 03:52.800
Her snorkel comes out of the water.

03:53.000 --> 03:56.800
Jen takes a big breath.

03:57.000 --> 04:01.800
She dives down under the water again.

04:02.000 --> 04:06.800
Jen swims past a large rock.

04:07.000 --> 04:09.700
Suddenly she stops.

04:10.000 --> 04:13.800
She sees a dolphin.

04:14.000 --> 04:15.650
It cannot swim.

04:15.750 --> 04:20.800
The dolphin is in a net.

04:21.000 --> 04:25.800
The net is around the dolphin's body.

04:26.000 --> 04:29.800
The net is around the rocks.

04:30.000 --> 04:34.800
The dolphin cannot swim up to get air.

04:35.000 --> 04:39.800
The beautiful blue dolphin is dying.

04:41.000 --> 04:44.800
The dolphin moves its fins slowly.

04:45.000 --> 04:47.800
But the net is strong.

04:48.000 --> 04:51.800
The dolphin cannot break the net.

04:54.000 --> 04:57.800
"Hi, dolphin. I'll help you."

04:58.000 --> 05:01.800
Jen pulls the net from the rocks.

05:02.000 --> 05:05.800
She pulls the net from the dolphin.

05:06.000 --> 05:09.800
The dolphin is out of the net.

05:10.000 --> 05:13.800
The dolphin moves its fins quickly.

05:14.000 --> 05:16.800
It swims fast.

05:17.000 --> 05:20.800
The dolphin swims up and up.

05:21.000 --> 05:23.800
It takes a breath of air.

05:24.000 --> 05:27.800
The dolphin looks down at Jen.

05:28.000 --> 05:30.800
Then it swims away.

05:34.000 --> 05:35.950
Jen is happy.

05:36.000 --> 05:39.800
She tells Rick about the dolphin.

05:43.000 --> 05:45.950
Next day, everybody is swimming.

05:46.000 --> 05:48.800
No one is surfing.

05:49.000 --> 05:50.950
The sea is flat.

05:51.000 --> 05:54.800
The sun is high in the sky.

05:55.000 --> 05:59.800
The hot sun shines on the water.

06:00.000 --> 06:03.800
The water is silver and blue.

06:04.000 --> 06:09.800
Men, women and children are in the sea.

06:10.000 --> 06:13.800
They are playing and laughing.

06:14.000 --> 06:16.800
Everybody is happy.

06:17.000 --> 06:20.800
The lifeguard watches the sea.

06:21.000 --> 06:24.800
He looks at the people swimming.

06:25.000 --> 06:28.800
Suddenly he shouts loudly.

06:29.000 --> 06:34.800
"Shark! Quick! Get out of the water!"

06:35.000 --> 06:38.800
The shark is swimming quickly.

06:39.000 --> 06:40.800
It is hungry.

06:41.000 --> 06:44.800
Its black fin is above the water.

06:45.000 --> 06:49.500
The shark is swimming towards the people.

06:49.600 --> 06:52.800
Everybody is frightened.

06:53.000 --> 06:55.800
Sharks are dangerous.

06:56.000 --> 06:58.800
They have long, sharp teeth.

06:59.000 --> 07:03.800
Everybody swims towards the beach.

07:04.000 --> 07:09.800
Jen and Rick are swimming a long way from the beach.

07:10.000 --> 07:13.800
The shark comes towards Rick.

07:14.000 --> 07:16.950
Jen is very frightened.

07:17.000 --> 07:18.800
She shouts at Rick.

07:19.000 --> 07:22.700
"Rick! Look out!"

07:22.800 --> 07:28.600
Rick sees the shark's black fin above the water.

07:28.700 --> 07:32.000
The shark is 30 meters away.

07:33.000 --> 07:36.800
Jen and Rick swim towards the beach.

07:37.000 --> 07:41.800
Now the shark is 15 meters away.

07:42.000 --> 07:47.800
Jen can see the shark's sharp white teeth.

07:48.000 --> 07:52.800
Suddenly they see another fin in the water.

07:53.000 --> 07:54.800
A blue fin.

07:55.000 --> 07:57.800
It is a dolphin.

07:58.000 --> 08:01.800
It is the beautiful blue dolphin.

08:02.000 --> 08:06.800
The dolphin is swimming towards the shark.

08:07.000 --> 08:09.800
The dolphin hits the shark.

08:10.000 --> 08:18.800
The dolphin hits the shark again and again.

08:18.900 --> 08:21.800
The shark swims away.

08:21.900 --> 08:22.800
Rick and Jen are safe.

08:24.000 --> 08:25.800
"Look, Rick!"

08:26.000 --> 08:31.800
"It's my blue dolphin."

08:32.000 --> 08:38.800
"Thanks, dolphin. Thanks for saving us."

08:39.000 --> 09:02.800
Blue Fins by Sarah Axton